			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864036">
									

<p>In the tale itself, you should probably develop in the writing who the protagonist holds allegiance to as the events unfold. Does he hold sympathy towards them, is he still set on getting them into containment, or is he just waiting it out to get away? Why are the lights telling him all this information?<br />
When it comes to the SCP: What is the danger or interesting aspects of these lights themselves? Is this location the lights take him to also a factor in the SCP? The SCP log would benefit if it contains the Foundation's management of the damages if at all. If the foundation is entirely unable to contain, influence, or mitigate the SCP's exposure to the outside world, it just feels sort of useless to read as part of the SCP foundation unless it's tied into other portions of the foundation. I could see potential tie-ins with SCP-1000, MTF Ghost busters, MTF Mole Rats, MTF City Slickers, and MTF White Rabbits if you're comfortable with them. Make sure to include how they are managed by the foundation to the best or their ability.</p>

							</div>

								
					
