									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karablue9482" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7130109); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7130109&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609987886" alt="Karablue9482" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7130109)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karablue9482" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7130109); return false;" >Karablue9482</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609984141 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Jan 2021 01:49</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-891087/help:questions-desk">Writing Help / Help: Questions Desk</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13971592/how-many-times-should-i-ask-for-a-critique">How many times should I ask for a critique?</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864013">
									

<p>If they leave a placeholder and a time (Such as &quot;Will crit within 24 hours&quot;) you can PM them after the time is up to remind them. If they don't respond, don't spam them with requests. If they've critiqued your idea and you've edited it, you can PM them again to see if they'll take another look. If someone tells you no or that they're busy, stop asking them since they're probably busy or just don't want to review it. Honestly, if you act respectfully towards the people doing you a favor, they'll have no issue critiquing you further, assuming time/life/whatever allows.</p>
<p>I suggest PMing more people (that you think, based on the butt squad roster, will be a good fit for critting) and stopping by our <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/chat-guide">Crit Chat</a> (#thecritters, the guide I linked there will teach you everything.) There are a lot more reviewers than just the ones on the butterfly squad roster that will help out there.</p>
<p>I hope this helped!</p>

